# champ-health targets — one line per public surface that must stay up.
#   name | url | expected HTTP status | must-contain string (optional)
#
# The must-contain string is what turns "the server answered" into "the server
# answered CORRECTLY" — a 200 that serves the wrong build is still an outage.
# Adding a new tool is one line here; nothing else changes.

# ── ChampBeam ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ChampBeam API (share.lakeb2b.com) | https://share.lakeb2b.com/health          | 200 | healthy
ChampBeam app (www.champbeam.com) | https://www.champbeam.com/                | 200 | Champbeam
ChampBeam VPS standby             | https://champbeam-api.64.227.154.215.sslip.io/health | 200 | healthy

# ── ChamPDF ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ChamPDF API                       | https://champdf-api.64.227.154.215.sslip.io/api/capabilities | 200 |
ChamPDF app (Vercel)              | https://cham-pdf.vercel.app/              | 200 |
# champdf.com currently has an EMPTY DNS zone (nameservers moved to InboxKit and the
# records were never recreated), so this check fails for a real reason. Leave it on:
# it is the only thing that will tell you the day it comes back — or goes dark again.
ChamPDF site (champdf.com)        | https://champdf.com/                      | 200 |

# ── Champ workspace / BearDrive ──────────────────────────────────────────────
Champ workspace                   | https://champ-workspace.64.227.154.215.sslip.io/api/health | 200 |
BearDrive                         | https://bdrive.64.227.154.215.sslip.io/health | 200 |

# ── Deepify (Coolify control plane) ──────────────────────────────────────────
Deepify                           | https://deepify.64.227.154.215.sslip.io/api/health | 200 |

